From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 02:00:00 -0700
Subject: cam: icp: keep FW alive after the boot-time download

The ICP FW dies with SFR "ICP SS WD Timeout" at a constant ~0.775 s
after its first boot, regardless of whether the boot-time power
collapse uses the hard-close path or (with icp_pc_en) the proper
PC_PREP handshake + proc_suspend: on this mainline port the ICP
watchdog keeps counting through the collapsed state and kills the
next instance at resume/re-download time (BPS acquire then fails
MEM_MAP -110 against a dead FW).

Sidestep the WDT-across-PC problem for bring-up: skip the power
collapse cam_icp_mgr_hw_open performs right after the boot-time
download, leaving the FW running (it services its own watchdog).
Acquire then takes the "FW already downloaded" path with a healthy
instance. IPE/BPS core clocks are still deinited. Proper PC/resume
can be revisited once the WDT clock/reset wiring across collapse is
understood.
---

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
index 8c98e0d..f7fc3cc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
@@ -3856,8 +3856,7 @@ static int cam_icp_mgr_hw_open(void *hw_mgr_priv, void *download_fw_args)
 		return rc;
 
 	rc = cam_ipe_bps_deint(hw_mgr);
-	rc = cam_icp_mgr_icp_power_collapse(hw_mgr);
-	CAM_DBG(CAM_ICP, "deinit all clocks at boot up");
+	pr_err("vamos-icp: keeping FW alive after boot download (skip boot-time power collapse)\n");
 
 	return rc;
 
